nt and future 3e Sidereal players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T10:38:02-07:00","id":1443137,"title":"","content":"The different Astrology things are an interesting take, but the fairly strict dicepools feel a bit limiting, especially with RDs demanding Craft Artifact. Allowing some wiggle room in the Attribute, the Ability, or both might be helpful. I could see perhaps allowing Wits and/or Survival for Star Charts, for example. The fact that your version of the Sidereal Excellency seems to be applicable regardless of Attribute or Ability might soften it a bit, but it feels a little restrictive for something that seems like a core Sidereal thing, especially for RDs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-08T12:41:03-07:00","id":1443155,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback.<br /> <br /> I have run a Sidereal with Craft: Artifact: 0 who utilizes 